<h2>Coral Reef</h2>
<p>Natural underwater reef structures made from secretion by living corals called exoskeletons which support and protect their bodies. Coral reefs are actually large colonies of tiny living animals found in marine waters that contain few nutrients. Most coral reefs are built from stony corals, which in turn consist of polypus that cluster in groups. Reefs grow best in warm, shallow, clear, sunny and agitated waters. Here in the Keys, we have the largest, living coral reef in North America, extending for more than 190 miles. Just inside of the main reef, we also have what is known as patch reefs, small almost circular coral formations that hole fish</p>
</div>
